Event / Info:
Hillel International, the Anti-Defamation League (ADL), and related nonprofits release recommendations to combat antisemitism on university campuses. Key points include:
(1) Clearly communicate campus rules, standards, and policies;
(2) Support Jewish students, including by providing antisemitism education and training;
(3) Ensure campus safety, including by enforcing codes of conduct and reaffirming “rejection of BDS and academic boycotts of Israel”;
(4) Reaffirm faculty responsibilities for “students’ academic freedom and a non-discriminatory learning environment in the classroom”;
(5) Prepare for disruptions on the anniversary of October 7 to ensure “any protest activities do not interfere with campus operations or Jewish students’ rights.”
